 "notes": "Captions-only packet with no synthesis, no motivation text and no control electrode (no bare SnO2 or SnO2/RGO cycling curve), so the design benefit is argued, not contrasted. Spine: need -> binding hypothesis -> NC@N-RGO architecture -> synthesis -> rutile 4-6 nm SnO2, carbon-skin encapsulation and interfacial binding -> ~1100 mAh g-1 capacity -> two branches: long cycling (explained by buffering MEC m1) and high rate (explained by short-path MEC m2, argued from KNW k3) -> conclusion. Audits: o13 (capacity climbs above the early reversible value over 500 cycles) and o16 (cycled material is a compact agglomerate) qualify m1; o15 and o8 carry partial image_support. Packet problems: F4 caption spans are shifted by one panel (F4a 'EDX spectrum' is the STEM image, F4b 'and carbon' is the EDX spectrum, and so on); F4i OCR letter reads 'D' but the crop is (i); F1a is labelled with the high-magnification span; F1c, F1d and F3d author-written indices and labels are only partly in the annotation lists.",
